⧗-26.392 · read from the running system, every claim checkable

── TODAY · what actually happens ──────────────────────────────

  systemd --user
  ~/.config/systemd/user/tpr.service        ← vec3 law forbids
      │                                       this location
      │ ExecStart
      ▼
  TPR.Gen/.venv/bin/python3 -u run.py       ← 123 KB of Python
      │
      ├─1 locate station   TPR_HOME → .station/
      ├─2 load::lock       .station/tpr/lock3ox.kdl → 10 tiers
      │                    then the token from
      │                    .station/vec3/lib/keys/Ender_Zen
      │                    (missing token = hard stop, only one)
      ├─3 identity         7HE.ENDER/.3ox/.ae/Ender.ae
      │                    + tpr.spark + Ender.sparkfile
      │                    = SYSTEM_PROMPT
      ├─4 webhook          setWebhook + getMe
      └─5 listen           :7089

  NO run.rb. NO brains. NO .rs. NO Brains/ folder.
  The TPR tree holds: run.py · kappa.py · streaming.py ·
  loop_controller.py · webapp/ · .station/{tpr,vec3/lib}
:: ∎

── THE 3OX SHAPE · what a cube boots like ─────────────────────

  1-Spark → 2-Brains → 3-Rules → 4-Toolkit → 5-Links → 6-Pulse
              │
              └─ 2-Brains/rust ──brains-build──► vec3/bin/brains
                                                 (static musl ELF)
  vec3/rc/run.rb   ruby · verbs: boot|ack|paths|status
                   writes vec3/proc/<port>
                   LAW: no tool may REQUIRE run.rb
                        (one exception: the brains compile)
:: ∎

── THE GAP · why the chain in your head is not on disk ────────

  A cube has six numbered faces. TPR is not a cube — it is a
  STATION, and its .station/ holds two things only: the lock
  (tpr/) and the keyring (vec3/lib). There is no face 2, so
  there is nothing for brains to be, and nothing calls run.rb.

  So `tpr.service → Brains/brain.rs → run.rb` is a TARGET, not
  a trace. To make it real, three things must exist that do not:
    a station-shaped set of six faces under station names
    a compiled face 2 for the station (its own brains-build)
    a boot verb that writes proc/ for a station, not a cube
:: ∎

── 100 YEAR TEST · what survives, what rots ───────────────────

  survives   KDL that declares shape · a static musl binary ·
             plain text cards · a port map
  rots       Python + a venv (interpreter drifts) · JSON packs ·
             a unit file in ~/.config/systemd/user · three
             registries claiming three different homes for the
             same station
  wire law   JSON is the Telegram API's language, not ours —
             it belongs at the send boundary, rendered from KDL,
             never as the thing a human edits
:: ∎

── PORT BAND · xxx0 + five ────────────────────────────────────

  :7080-7084  STORE.CC   (taken · CISA-0 Observe)
  :7090-7094  TPR        ← the next free start-on-zero pentad
      7090  0 Observe   the door · health · webhook in
      7091  1 Relate    .Gen · the relay itself
      7092  2 Infer     model reach
      7093  3 Weigh     routing · being resolution
      7094  4 Remember  spool · history
  ONE thing sits in the way: :7094 = ender-trainview (declared,
  own systemd unit). It is a telemetry view → digit 7 → :7087,
  which is free. One unit edit and the pentad is clean.
  Also squatting the band undeclared: :7078 and :7099, both
  `python3 -m http.server` static servers.
:: ∎
